UID:adina-talve-goodman-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190114Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:Deadline: One Story: Adina Talve-Goodman Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Annual educational fellowship honouring the memory of author an
 d former One Story managing editor Adina Talve-Goodman: a year-long mentor
 ship on the craft of fiction writing with One Story magazine\, aimed at gi
 ving a writer outside the fold a significant career boost. WHAT THE FELLOW
  RECEIVES: access to One Story online classes\; admission to the Writing C
 ircle\; a USD 2\,000 stipend and free admission to the week-long summer wr
 iters' conference with craft lectures\, an intensive fiction workshop and 
 panels with literary agents and publishers\; and a full manuscript review 
 and consultation with executive editor Hannah Tinti (story collection or n
 ovel in progress up to 150 pages / 35\,000 words). ELIGIBILITY: early-care
 er fiction writers who have not yet published a book\, have never been enr
 olled in an advanced degree programme (MA or MFA) in creative writing\, En
 glish or literature and have no plans to attend one in 2027\, and are at l
 east 21 years old as of 1 January 2027. Applicants outside the United Stat
 es are welcome. The fellowship seeks writing that centres\, celebrates or 
 reclaims being marginalised through the lens of race\, ethnicity\, gender\
 , sexuality\, age\, class\, religion\, illness\, disability\, trauma\, mig
 ration\, displacement\, dispossession or imprisonment. APPLY via Submittab
 le with a fiction sample of 3\,000 to 5\,000 words (multiple stories allow
 ed within the limit\, one file)\, a personal statement of 400 to 750 words
 \, a statement of purpose of 200 to 350 words\, two references (contact de
 tails only\, no letters) and a current resume including writing classes\, 
 awards\, publications and residencies. Applications open 8 September and c
 lose 13 October 2026 at 23:59 ET\; the winner is announced in January 2027
 .\n\nOrganisation: One Story (with the Talve-Goodman Family)\nLocation: Re
 mote year-long mentorship with One Story magazine (Brooklyn\, US)\; includ
 es free admission to the week-long summer writers' conference. Open to app
 licants outside the United States.\nAward: USD 2\,000 stipend plus free ad
 mission to One Story's week-long summer writers' conference\, access to On
 e Story online classes\, admission to the Writing Circle\, and a full manu
 script review and consultation with Executive Editor Hannah Tinti (story c
 ollection or novel in progress up to 150 pages / 35\,000 words). No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Year-long fellowship for 2027. Applications open 8 S
 eptember 2026 and close 13 October 2026 at 23:59 ET\; winner announced pub
 licly in January 2027.\n\nMore: https://one-story.com/learn/fellowship/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://one-story.com/learn/fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote year-long mentorship with One Story magazine (Brooklyn\, US
 )\; includes free admission to the week-long summer writers' conference. O
 pen to applicants outside the United States.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
